  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The novel treats refinement path as a named cultivation path with Gu Masters, Immortal Gu, attainment ranks, and path styles. Process detail, recipes, fusion steps, and material ranks live on Gu refinement, separate from refinement path itself as a cultivation line.",
      "chapters": [],
      "certainty": "inferred",
      "confidence": "C",
      "verification": "no_citation",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "fac_gu_masters",
        "sys_immortal_gu",
        "sys_refinement"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Among the three kings, King Xin was a refinement path Gu Master, and his inheritance selected inheritors who followed that path.",
      "chapters": [
        347
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "what-the-path-governs",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_king_xin",
        "sys_gu_master"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Advance refinement Gu is named a refinement path Immortal Gu, and refinement path immortal materials are easier for a refinement path specialist to process than wood path immortal materials such as those of Heavenly Essence Treasure Imperial Lotus.",
      "chapters": [
        2250
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "what-the-path-governs",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "gu_advance_refinement_gu",
        "gu_heavenly_essence_treasure_lotus"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Throughout history, refinement path had two styles. The first was the hairy man nature Gu refinement method, which used nature and dao marks to refine Gu, with Limitless Demon Venerable’s use of Gu worms to refine heaven and earth as its opposite. The second was the human isolation style. Ni clan’s Gu Immortal, the refinement path quasi-supreme Ni Ren, used humans to refine Gu and implanted Immortal Gu in Ni clan bloodlines, with methods that use Gu to refine human as the opposite side of that style. Fang Yuan evaluates that the depth of refinement path supreme grandmaster should likely comprise those four aspects, and that after Human Sea and Limitless Demon Venerable’s arrangements he still needs to finish comprehending using Gu to refine heaven and earth.",
      "chapters": [
        2168
      ],
      "certainty": "inferred",
      "confidence": "C",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "two-historical-styles",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "gu_nature_gu_refinement_technique",
        "char_limitless_demon_venerable",
        "sys_gu_worms",
        "fac_ni_clan",
        "sys_gu_immortal",
        "char_ni_ren",
        "char_fang_yuan",
        "loc_human_sea"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "A Thieving Heaven true inheritance portion adds refining fake Gu as a further refinement path aspect beyond those four.",
      "chapters": [
        2178
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "two-historical-styles",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "inh_thieving_heaven_true_inheritance"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan is a refinement path venerable, and refining Immortal Gu is extremely easy for him at that stage.",
      "chapters": [
        2250
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "refinement-path-venerable",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    }
